# graywolf pin side constraints for snake_chip
#
# This file places the CORE's signal pins only.  Power is not named here and
# cannot be: inside the core it arrives on the rails and the stripes that
# `addspacers -stripe 8 225 PG` builds, and around the core it arrives through
# the PADVDD/PADGND cells placed in ../chip_top.  No .cel2 in this design kit
# mentions vdd or gnd.
#
# ---- how a side becomes a package pin -------------------------------------
#
# MPW_PAD_28Pin_IO.mag has seven pad slots per side, named PAD_0..PAD_27 - an
# empty template, which is what makes a custom pinout possible at all.
# MPW_PAD_28Pin_IO_Games.mag is the same frame already filled in, and reading
# it against MyChip_Game_Package.txt pins the correspondence down exactly:
#
#     side L -> package pins  1..7        side R -> package pins 15..21
#     side B -> package pins  8..14       side T -> package pins 22..28
#
# ---- why one group per side ------------------------------------------------
#
# Twelve signals and sixteen power pads have to share 28 slots.  The Games
# part puts every signal on T and B and fills L and R with power, so current
# enters the ring from two opposite sides only.  Spreading the signals over
# all four sides leaves 2/3/5/6 free slots per side instead, so the power pads
# spread too and the ring is fed from four sides - worth having with ~2400
# cells switching at 25MHz.
#
# Grouping is the other half of the point.  A padgroup is what keeps pads
# adjacent, so the five joystick lines come out as five consecutive package
# pins and go to one connector, and so do the panel lines.  One group per pin
# would ask graywolf for nothing.
#
# permute is deliberately omitted: with it, graywolf may reorder the pads
# inside a group, and the joystick is far easier to wire in UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT
# order.  Confirm what actually came out in layout/snake_chip.pin after
# `make place`; grouping holds either way, only the order within a group
# depends on this.
#
# Run `make check_pins` after editing - a misspelt twpin_ name is not an error
# to graywolf, the pin simply goes back to being unconstrained.

# ---- side T, package pins 22..28 : the 5-way switch ------------------------
padgroup Joystick
twpin_JS_UP                     nonfixed
twpin_JS_DOWN                   nonfixed
twpin_JS_LEFT                   nonfixed
twpin_JS_RIGHT                  nonfixed
twpin_JS_OK                     nonfixed
restrict side T

# ---- side R, package pins 15..21 : the panel ------------------------------
#
# SCL_OE, SDA_OE and SDA_I are three core ports that become two PADINOUT cells
# at chip_top (DO tied low, OEN driven, DI read back), so they have to sit
# next to each other or the pad ring wiring gets long.
padgroup OLED_I2C
twpin_SCL_OE                    nonfixed
twpin_SDA_OE                    nonfixed
twpin_SDA_I                     nonfixed
twpin_OLED_RES_N                nonfixed
restrict side R

# ---- side B, package pins 8..14 : oscillator and reset --------------------
padgroup System
twpin_CLK                       nonfixed
twpin_RST_N                     nonfixed
restrict side B

# ---- side L, package pins 1..7 : heartbeat --------------------------------
padgroup Status
twpin_LED                       nonfixed
restrict side L
